[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (-1.0,0) -- (-1.0,2.5);
\draw (1.0,0) -- (1.0,2.5);
\draw (-1.0,0) arc (180:360:1.0 and 0.3);
\draw[dashed] (1.0,0) arc (0:180:1.0 and 0.3);
\draw (-1.0,2.5) arc (180:360:1.0 and 0.3);
\draw[dashed] (1.0,2.5) arc (0:180:1.0 and 0.3);
\draw (-1.0,2.5) arc (180:0:1.0);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.2pt);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,0)--(1.0,0) node[midway,below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$2\text{ cm}$};
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-1.35,0)--(-1.35,2.5) node[midway,left] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A solid trophy is a hemisphere on top of a closed cylinder of radius $2$ cm and height $5$ cm. Find its total surface area, correct to $2$ decimal places.

